---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Method from '../components/Method.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Layout title="Work with me | Pranjal Pandey" description="AI strategy, workflow audits, builds and advisory for companies; focused 1:1 AI strategy and career sessions for founders, leaders and individuals.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">For companies & leadership teams</p><h1>Work with me</h1><p class="lead">I work with founders, managers and leadership teams who've seen what AI could do and now need it to work for real.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/call/">Book a call <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a><span class="fine-print">Free 30-minute intro call. No pitch deck needed.</span></div></header>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-intro"><h2>Start with the problem.<br />Scope the work from there.</h2><p>These are engagement shapes, not fixed packages or guaranteed timelines. Scope, fees and availability are agreed before work starts.</p></div>
      <article class="service"><div><span class="mono">01 / Free intro</span><h3>Unstick your AI pilot.</h3></div><div><p>For leaders with a stalled AI pilot, a messy process, or a "should we even use AI for this?" question.</p><p><strong>You get:</strong> an honest first read on what's blocking you, and a short written follow-up with the next step.</p><a class="text-link" href="/call/">Book a free 30-minute call</a></div></article>
      <article class="service"><div><span class="mono">02 / Workshop</span><h3>Leadership AI workshop</h3></div><div><p>For leadership teams who need a shared view of where AI fits before they spend money.</p><p><strong>You get:</strong> a half- or full-day working session on your business, a shortlist of AI opportunities ranked by value and risk, and a 90-day plan.</p><p>Fixed fee, quoted per team.</p></div></article>
      <article class="service"><div><span class="mono">03 / Audit</span><h3>AI Workflow Audit</h3></div><div><p>For companies who know AI could help but aren't sure where to start, or have too many ideas and no priorities.</p><p><strong>You get:</strong> a map of how one or two teams work today, the three workflows where AI pays off most ranked by impact and effort, and an architecture and 90-day plan you can build on, with me or without me.</p><p>A two-week engagement, scoped on a free intro call and confirmed in a written fixed-fee proposal.</p></div></article>
      <article class="service"><div><span class="mono">04 / Build</span><h3>Build it with me</h3></div><div><p>For teams ready to take one workflow to production.</p><p><strong>You get:</strong> a working workflow in your systems, including agents, integrations, evaluation and human approval steps, and a team that knows how to run it.</p><p>A four-to-eight-week starting scope. Timing and fees are agreed after the audit, based on access, integrations and complexity.</p></div></article>
      <article class="service"><div><span class="mono">05 / Advise</span><h3>Fractional AI advisor</h3></div><div><p>For startups and companies who need senior AI strategy and architecture judgment, but not a full-time hire.</p><p><strong>You get:</strong> two to four days a month of strategy, architecture reviews, tool and vendor decisions, and team guidance.</p><p>Monthly retainer. Cadence, availability and fees are agreed together.</p></div></article>
      <article class="service"><div><span class="mono">Also available</span><h3>Applied R&D</h3></div><div><p>For harder problems like task allocation, scheduling, optimisation or getting multiple agents to coordinate. That's where the research side of my life comes in handy.</p><a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email me with the problem</a></div></article>
    </section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-intro"><h2>Diagnose. Decide. Build.</h2><p>A working method across engagements, with the depth matched to your situation.</p></div><Method /></section>
    <section class="section" id="sessions">
      <div class="section-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">For founders & individuals</p><h2>A focused question.<br />Dedicated time.</h2></div><p>These are paid working sessions, separate from the free company intro call. Current prices, availability and booking terms are shown on Topmate.</p></div>
      <article class="offer-row"><span class="mono">90 minutes</span><div><h3>AI Strategy Planning</h3><p>For founders and business teams who want a clear AI plan without a full audit. A prep questionnaire, 90 focused minutes, and a written 30/60/90-day AI plan within 48 hours. The fee is credited toward an Audit if you go ahead within 30 days.</p></div><a class="text-link" href={site.strategy}>Book a strategy session <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></article>
      <article class="offer-row"><span class="mono">60 minutes</span><div><h3>AI Career & Portfolio Kickstart</h3><p>For professionals and serious students moving into AI and workflow automation. A clear direction for your background, two or three portfolio project ideas that show real skill, what to learn next and what to skip, and a written summary.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/session/">Book a career session <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></article>
      <p>Not ready for a session? <a href="/guides/#free-guide">Start with the free guide</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-intro"><h2>A useful fit matters.</h2><p>I work best with teams ready to name the problem, involve the people doing the work and make the trade-offs explicit.</p></div>
      <div class="faq">
        <details><summary>What happens on the free intro call?</summary><p>We use 30 minutes to understand your workflow and what's blocking it. You get an honest first read and a short written follow-up with the next step. Paid sessions are dedicated planning time.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do you work with clients outside India?</summary><p>Yes. I work remotely with teams in India and abroad.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What if I'm not sure AI is the answer?</summary><p>Then that's the first thing we'll figure out. Sometimes the honest answer is "not yet".</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do you speak at events?</summary><p>Yes. See the <a href="/press/">Press & speaking page</a> for topics and contact details.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can you work with our existing team?</summary><p>Yes. The work can complement an internal delivery team. Ownership, access and handover are part of the scope, not details to resolve at the end.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can you guarantee ROI or a production launch?</summary><p>No. Results depend on the workflow, data, integrations and adoption. We agree evaluation criteria and a realistic scope before committing to implementation.</p></details>
        <details><summary>When is this not a fit?</summary><p>If you're looking for a guaranteed return, a model demo with no workflow owner, or a tool purchase before defining the problem, this is probably not the right engagement.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can we discuss confidential work?</summary><p>Start with a non-sensitive description. We can agree the appropriate confidentiality and access arrangements before exchanging private data or internal materials.</p></details>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="close"><h2>Bring the workflow.<br />We'll start there.</h2><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/call/">Book a free intro call</a><a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email me instead</a></div></section>
  </div>
</Layout>
